    <string name="faq_accessibility_q">Why does Slate need Accessibility permission?</string>
    <string name="faq_accessibility_a">Only double-tap to lock uses the accessibility service. It invokes Android\'s lock-screen action and does not read screen content.</string>
    <string name="faq_data_q">Does Slate collect any data?</string>
    <string name="faq_data_a">No. Slate is offline, has no analytics or tracking, and keeps settings and usage counts on your device.</string>
    <string name="faq_permissions_q">What permissions does Slate use?</string>
    <string name="faq_permissions_a">Permissions support the features you choose: listing apps, opening system panels, uninstall confirmation, lock-screen wallpaper, biometric verification, and double-tap to lock. Slate does not request contacts or phone-call access.</string>
    <string name="faq_hidden_q">How does the hidden apps lock work?</string>
    <string name="faq_hidden_a">You can require a PIN to view or unhide apps. Biometric unlock is optional, with the PIN as a fallback. The PIN is stored as a salted hash, never in plain text.</string>
    <string name="faq_menu_q">How does the long-press menu lock work?</string>
    <string name="faq_menu_a">When enabled, opening home, app, folder, or shortcut menus and using the Open settings gesture requires the same PIN. This lock does not use biometric unlock.</string>
    <string name="faq_recents_q">Do hidden apps appear in Recents?</string>
    <string name="faq_recents_a">By default, Slate launches hidden apps outside Recents. You can change this in Security if you need those apps to stay open when switching away. An existing task opened elsewhere may still appear until you remove it from Recents.</string>
    <string name="faq_folders_q">How do folders work?</string>
    <string name="faq_folders_a">Long-press an app and choose Move to folder. Tap a folder to open it; long-press it to rename, recolor, pin, or delete it. Deleting a folder returns its apps to the main list.</string>
    <string name="faq_connectivity_q">Why can\'t Slate toggle Wi-Fi or Bluetooth directly?</string>
    <string name="faq_connectivity_a">Android restricts direct control of these radios for third-party apps. Slate opens the appropriate system panel or settings page without asking for broader access.</string>
    <string name="faq_source_q">Is Slate open source?</string>
    <string name="faq_source_a">Yes. Slate is released under the MIT license. Source: github.com/roufsyed/Slate-Minimal-Launcher</string>
    <string name="tour_welcome_title">Welcome to Slate</string>
    <string name="tour_welcome_body">Slate lists your apps as text. Here is a short guide.</string>
    <string name="tour_tap_title">Tap to open</string>
    <string name="tour_tap_body">Tap an app name to open it. You can sort the list by name or usage in Settings.</string>
    <string name="tour_app_menu_title">Long-press an app</string>
    <string name="tour_app_menu_body">Hold an app name to pin, hide, rename, recolor, move, or uninstall it.</string>
    <string name="tour_home_menu_title">Long-press the home screen</string>
    <string name="tour_home_menu_body">Hold a blank area for Customize, Hidden Apps, and FAQ.</string>
    <string name="tour_folder_title">Folders</string>
    <string name="tour_folder_body">Choose Move to folder from an app menu. Tap a folder to expand it.</string>
    <string name="tour_gestures_title">Swipe gestures</string>
    <string name="tour_gestures_body">Swipe in the directions you configured in Settings to run your chosen actions.</string>
    <string name="tour_lock_title">Double-tap to lock</string>
    <string name="tour_lock_body">Double-tap an empty area to lock the screen.</string>
    <string name="tour_custom_title">Customize more</string>
    <string name="tour_custom_body">Fonts, colors, gestures, security, theme, language, and backup are in Settings.</string>
    <string name="tour_done_title">You\'re set</string>
    <string name="tour_done_body">You can open this guide again from Settings → About.</string>
